<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Prince Louis of Battenberg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1854">1854</a>–<a href="/years/1921">1921</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Louis Mountbatten, 1st Marquess of Milford Haven</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Prince Louis of Battenberg was a German-born British admiral of the Hessian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battenberg-family">Battenberg family</a>. He joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-navy">Royal Navy</a> in 1868 and became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-sea-lord">First Sea Lord</a> in 1912, but resigned in 1914 because of anti-German feeling. In 1917 he gave up his German titles, took the name Mountbatten and became Marquess of Milford Haven; he was the father of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-mountbatten">Louis Mountbatten</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/prince-louis-of-battenberg.jpg" alt="Prince Louis of Battenberg" width="320" height="490" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1_milford-haven-1909.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
